From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] grt: store the maze's search directions in a byte
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

directions_3D_ holds one of seven directions per GCell and layer, in an
enum class with the default int underlying type: 4 bytes where 1 does.
On a 34 M GCell x 9 layer die that is about 0.9 GB less.

Carried in bazel-orfs for OpenROAD#12075, not upstreamed; retires with
the //:bump onto an OpenROAD that has it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
---
 src/grt/src/fastroute/include/DataType.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/grt/src/fastroute/include/DataType.h b/src/grt/src/fastroute/include/DataType.h
index 10b25dada1..cdd966b9ba 100644
--- a/src/grt/src/fastroute/include/DataType.h
+++ b/src/grt/src/fastroute/include/DataType.h
@@ -30,7 +30,7 @@ enum class RouteType
 
 std::ostream& operator<<(std::ostream& os, const RouteType& type);
 
-enum class Direction
+enum class Direction : uint8_t
 {
   North,
   East,
-- 
